.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt NVPTXAS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvptxas ,
.Nm ptxas
.Nd preserve PTX in the cuda-native assembler stub
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl m64
.Op Fl O Ns Ar level
.Fl -gpu-name
.Ar arch
.Fl -output-file
.Ar file
.Op Fl -
.Ar input.ptx
.Pp
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
and its installed alias
.Nm ptxas
are the same POSIX shell program.
They accept the option subset that clang 23 emits for a CUDA device compile.
The input must contain exactly one
.Li .target
line, and its architecture must equal
.Fl -gpu-name ;
a mismatch is refused with a diagnostic naming both.
.Pp
The output is a placeholder container whose first four lines are
.Bd -literal -offset indent
CUDA-NATIVE-STUB-CUBIN 1
arch=ARCH
ptx-sha256=HEX
---
.Ed
The complete PTX input follows the separator byte for byte.
The SHA-256 is taken over that unchanged PTX.
The container is written through a temporary file in the output directory and
renamed into place.
.Pp
The accepted compile options are
.Fl m64 ,
.Fl O0 ,
.Fl O1 ,
.Fl O2 ,
.Fl O3 ,
.Fl g ,
.Fl lineinfo ,
.Fl -dont-merge-basicblocks ,
.Fl -return-at-end ,
.Fl -gpu-name
and
.Fl -output-file .
The last two options also accept an equals sign between the option and its
value.
The architecture, output and one input are required.
The optional
.Fl -
argument ends option processing; every later argument is positional, and the
single input may therefore have a dash-prefixed name such as
.Pa -g .
A path such as
.Pa ./-g
also avoids option parsing without the delimiter.
.Fl h
and
.Fl -help
print usage.
Every argument that starts with a dash before
.Fl -
is parsed as an option, regardless of whether a same-named file exists.
Every unsupported option is refused instead of being ignored.
.Pp
.Fl -version
prints
.Ql nvptxas (cuda-native) VERSION stub .
With
.Fl -json
it prints one JSON object containing
.Dv tool ,
.Dv version ,
.Dv version_major ,
.Dv version_minor ,
.Dv version_patch ,
.Dv stub
and
.Dv track .
The version string and its three integer parts come from
.Dv CUDA_NATIVE_VERSION
in
.Pa sdk/include/cuda.h
when
.Pa mksdk.sh
installs the tool.
The object validates against
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/cuda-native-tool-1.schema.json .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CUDA_NATIVE_TRACE
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_TRACE
When nonempty, append one JSON record after a successful placeholder write.
The record has
.Dv tool ,
.Dv schema ,
.Dv arch ,
.Dv input ,
.Dv output
and
.Dv stub
fields, and is validated by
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/nvptxas-trace-1.schema.json
in the SDK tree.
Arguments containing control bytes or malformed UTF-8 are refused before
writing output or a trace.
Valid UTF-8 paths are accepted, and JSON metacharacters are escaped, keeping
every emitted string parseable as UTF-8 JSON.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
In detail, exit status 0 means that the placeholder was written, 2 reports
usage or an unsupported option, and 1 reports an input, architecture mismatch,
output or trace error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Preserve a PTX file under the name clang would use for an object:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ptxas -m64 -O0 --gpu-name sm_121 --output-file kernel.o kernel.ptx
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvfatbin 1 ,
.Xr libcudart-stub 3 ,
.Xr cuda-native-toolchain 7
.Sh CAVEATS
This is not an assembler.
The real assembler is Track #2427.
Its output is a cuda-native placeholder containing PTX text, not a real cubin
or other GPU machine code.
The explicit header prevents the payload from being mistaken for a bare PTX
file or an assembled cubin.
It permits clang's compile pipeline to finish without claiming that device code
can execute.
No NVIDIA CUDA toolkit file is used.
